@startuml tool-gate-at-a-glance
title The tool gate at a glance

left to right direction

rectangle "An agent wants to act\n\nfor example:\npay invoice INV-123\nto account X" as A

rectangle "The tool gate\n(K9-AIF 1.25.0)" as G {
  rectangle "1. Is it safe?\n\nsecurity checks\n(k9x Shield)" as S
  rectangle "2. Do the values match\nwhat we already know?\n\nthe vendor's account\non record" as R
  rectangle "3. What does the\nbusiness allow?\n\nthe company's own rules" as B
}

rectangle "Run it" as RUN
rectangle "Refuse it" as NO
rectangle "Ask a person\n\nshows exactly what will happen\nand what doesn't match" as P
rectangle "Approved: runs once\n\nAnything else:\nnever runs" as OUT

A --> S
S --> R
R --> B
B --> RUN : safe, matches,\nallowed
B --> NO : not allowed
B --> P : doesn't match,\nor can't be undone
P --> OUT

note bottom of G
  Every step is recorded:
  what was asked, what was decided,
  who approved it and when.
end note
@enduml
